;  979
;  980    ! FORMAT_VALUE shows a value: a real one as a number, a complex one as
;  981    ! a + bi. A part smaller than the other by more than the digits shown
;  982    ! is shown as zero: what the digits can't show. BESIDE, if it is given,
;  983    ! is a magnitude the parts are shown beside, so a part smaller than it by
;  984    ! more than the digits is shown as zero too: an element of a matrix is
;  985    ! shown beside the matrix's largest (module FCARRAYS). Under FIXED, a part
;  986    ! too small to show a digit is zero as well, so 1e-9 + 1e-6i is 0.0000.
;  987    ! A value whose parts are whole numbers is shown in NUMBER_BASE, exactly:
;  988    ! a whole number has no rounding to hide.
